NEARS-1486 QA [8] — PRE-EXISTING finding (NOT caused by this ticket)
Surface: UserApp -> store -> app-bar search -> StoreItemSearchScreen ("Price" DLS filter chip)
Device: emulator-5556 (Pixel_10_Pro_3, Android, light mode) | branch fix/NEARS-1486-dead-filter-chips @ b3372ea5
Store: Nears Mart (store_id=1, zone 1) | query: "o"

CLAIM: the surviving "Price" chip does NOT filter in-store search results. It is the same
dead-chip class this ticket removed ETA and Brand for. It was untouched by the diff, so it is
reported as a pre-existing defect, not a regression of this change.

--- 1. SOURCE: the in-store search request carries no discount/filter param ---
UserApp/lib/features/store/domain/repositories/store_repository.dart  (getStoreSearchItemList)

  Response response = await apiClient.getData(
    '${AppConstants.searchUri}items/search?store_id=$storeID&name=$searchText&offset=$offset&limit=10&type=$type&category_id=${categoryID ?? ''}',
  );

  -> params sent: store_id, name, offset, limit, type, category_id
  -> NO 'discounted' / 'filter' param exists on this call.

UserApp/lib/features/store/controllers/store_controller.dart

  void toggleDiscountedItems() {
    _isDiscountedItems = !_isDiscountedItems;
    if (_isDiscountedItems) { _filter!.add("discounted"); } else { _filter!.remove("discounted"); }
    update();
  }

  -> _filter is consumed by getStoreItemList (the store BROWSE grid, which does send
     &filter=$filterString) but is never read by getStoreSearchItemList. On the search
     screen the toggle therefore only flips the chip's own selected pixel state.

--- 2. LIVE: identical result set with the chip OFF and ON ---
Full scroll-through of the result list, both states, same query "o", same store:

  Price OFF : Brown Eggs, Cola 1.5L, Desi Cow Ghee, Dish Soap, Mango, Sample Product, Tomatoes, Watermelon   (8)
  Price ON  : Brown Eggs, Cola 1.5L, Desi Cow Ghee, Dish Soap, Mango, Sample Product, Tomatoes, Watermelon   (8)

  DELTA: none. Sets are identical.

  DB cross-check (read-only) — items.discount for those 8 rows:
    Tomatoes = 18.00 ; all seven others = 0.00
  i.e. 7 of 8 rows carry no item-level discount yet survive a "discounted" filter that
  is supposedly ON.

--- 3. CONTROL: the sibling chip on the same rail DOES filter ---
Same screen, same query, same run — "Organic" (which sends a real &type=veg param):

  Organic OFF : 8 items (list above)
  Organic ON  : Brown Eggs, Cola 1.5L, Dish Soap, Mango, Tomatoes, Watermelon           (6)
  DELTA: -2, exactly the two items with items.veg = 0 (Desi Cow Ghee, Sample Product).

  So the instrument (query, refetch, list re-render, dump) is proven live: it CAN show a
  result-set change on this exact screen. The Price no-delta is a real no-delta, not a
  dead measurement.

--- 4. NETWORK LOG for the Price tap (refetch fires, filter is absent) ---
  I/flutter (12918): [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/items/search
  I/flutter (12918): [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/items/search http_status=200
  (no [ERR] / [FAIL] — the call succeeds, it just carries no discount predicate)

--- 5. Same behaviour reproduced in RTL/Arabic ("سعر") and on a second store (Tower Mart, id 38).
